Carlos "Gu?no" Grohmann wrote:
> Tryed. didn't work..
>
> OK_pred_md250 <- krige(band1 ~ 1, srtm2, mask_SG, model=vrg.eye, 
> maxdist=250);
>
> Error in model.frame(formula, rownames, variables, varnames, extras,
> extranames,  :
>        invalid variable type for 'band1'
>
> Why do you think that the nugget variance would change anything?
Because the Gaussian variogram model is known to often lead to 
near-singular covariance matrices, meaning numerical instabilities, huge 
kriging weights etc.
--
Edzer
